WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.457
Apollo Q Labs. Level one: Foundations.

2
00:00:04.757 --> 00:00:12.503
What an option is, a contract on one hundred shares, how it is priced, and how to read the dashboard, the screen that sums up your trade.

3
00:00:12.503 --> 00:00:25.517
Module one: What an option is. Calls, the right to buy 100 shares at the strike, puts, the right to sell 100 shares at the strike, and what happens at expiration, the option’s last day.

4
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:38.511
Module two: Moneyness and value. Whether an option has value if used now, and how the premium, the price of an option, splits into that and time value, the part of the price paid for the chance of a bigger move.

5
00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:50.501
Module three: Buying, selling and implied volatility, or I V, the expected yearly move priced into options. Who carries which risk, and what I V says about price.

6
00:00:50.501 --> 00:01:09.895
Module four: Reading the dashboard. Cash paid or received, max profit and loss, break-even, the stock price at expiration where profit or loss is zero, probability of profit (the model’s estimate of the chance the trade makes money at expiration), and the payout chart, profit or loss by price.

7
00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.095
Start with module one.

